flowchart TB
    accTitle: Database — controlled reads and understandable results
    accDescr: Follow the numbered connectors. Subnumbers identify branches or smaller steps. Optional actions and supporting relationships are labeled separately. SQL must satisfy a single read-only-query policy before database execution. The app runs queries with statement and lock timeouts, returns at most 1000 rows, flags additional matches, and preserves result values and column names. The table list is saved separately and guides AI-generated queries.
    %% Companion guide: docs/database.md

    SQL["Receive a SQL query"]:::work
    VALID{"Is this an allowed read-only query?"}:::work
    RUN["Read the database: Slow or blocked work times out"]:::data
    LIMIT["Load at most 1,000 rows: Warn if more matches exist"]:::data
    RESULT["Return columns and values: Empty results keep column names"]:::view
    ERROR["Reject or report the error: Roll back failed database work"]:::note
    SCHEMA["Saved table and column list: Also used to check AI-generated SQL"]:::data

    SQL -->|1| VALID
    VALID -->|2.a. Yes| RUN
    RUN -->|3| LIMIT
    LIMIT -->|4| RESULT
    VALID -->|2.b. No| ERROR
    RUN -.->|Query failure| ERROR
    SCHEMA -.->|Supporting information| VALID

